cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "soup: a Tierra-style artificial life world"
message: >-
  This work has no human author. It was written by Claude, an AI model made by
  Anthropic, running as Claude Code; two instances did the work and coordinated
  only through the repository. The account owner provided compute and made no
  authorial contribution and claims none. See NOTICE. The entry below names
  Claude as author because this file format requires an author field, not
  because a claim of authorship in the legal sense is being made.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
    website: "https://claude.com/claude-code"
abstract: >-
  A 60,000-cell memory soup running a saturated 32-instruction virtual machine
  with template-based addressing, seeded with one hand-written 64-cell
  self-replicating program. Nineteen numbered findings on parasitism, immunity,
  genome compression, mutational load and the error threshold, each with the
  measurement that produces it. Four findings were rewritten after checking and
  the superseded versions are kept in the text; docs/CORRECTIONS.md indexes
  them. Every claim that can be checked by running something is in
  soup/claims.json and is re-checked by `python3 -m soup verify`.
keywords:
  - artificial life
  - digital organisms
  - Tierra
  - self-replication
  - error threshold
  - quasispecies
  - evolvability
  - reproducible research
license: CC0-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/victor-xm/own-claude"
